<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Independent Commission of Experts</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1996–2002</span> · Also known as Bergier Commission, Independent Commission of Experts Switzerland – Second World War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Independent Commission of Experts, known as the Bergier Commission, was set up by the Swiss parliament in 1996 and chaired by the historian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-francois-bergier">Jean-François Bergier</a> to investigate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>'s role in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. Its reports, the last appearing in 2002, examined gold purchases from Nazi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, dormant accounts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holocaust">Holocaust</a> victims and the turning back of refugees, and prompted a wide reassessment of the period.</p></div>
